{"id":1568,"date":"2020-12-02T12:13:37","date_gmt":"2020-12-02T20:13:37","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1568"},"modified":"2024-08-27T12:53:26","modified_gmt":"2024-08-27T19:53:26","slug":"codrone-blockly-jr-loops","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-jr-loops\/","title":{"rendered":"Loops"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b94a2\" name=\"6a221541b94a2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are loops?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Loops let you repeat sections of your code. They\u2019re a great shortcut &#8212; without them, you might have to connect the same blocks over and over again! Blockly has three different types of loops:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For loops will repeat the code inside them for the number of times you choose. There are two blocks that do this! <\/span><\/li>\n<li>While loops will repeat the code inside them while a certain condition that you set is true.<\/li>\n<li>Until loops will repeat the code inside them until a certain condition that you set is true.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1569&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b9850\" name=\"6a221541b9850\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>For loops<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For loops repeat the code that\u2019s inside them for the number of times that you choose. Once that code has been repeated for that amount of time, your program will exit out of the loop and move on to the next block.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Like we said in the first step, there are two for loop blocks in Blockly! One is the repeat for _ times block. To change the number in that block, you can just type in a new value. If you want to use a mathematical operation, equation, or variable, you can drag blocks from the math, logic, or variables menus to that gray area within the loop block. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1570&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The other for loop block is a little more complicated and looks more like what you would see in text-based coding. With this block, you would name a variable, and then you would set it to start at one number and go up to another. You can also set how much you want the value to increase by. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1571&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b98c1\" name=\"6a221541b98c1\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a for loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ready to try for loops out? Program your CoDrone to look like it\u2019s flying up a flight of stairs! The catch: since there are two different for loop blocks, you will need to write two different programs to try them out. Your CoDrone should keep moving forward and up. The programs might look different to you, but what happens when you run them?<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1572&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1573&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b9918\" name=\"6a221541b9918\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>While loops<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While loops repeat the code that\u2019s inside them while the condition that you set is true. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each time the program<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">runs through the while loop, it checks to see if the condition is true. If it is not, your program will exit the loop.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1574&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b9992\" name=\"6a221541b9992\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a while loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You had your drone fly in a shape in the variables lesson, but now you can try it with a loop! Set your variable<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to 0, and then have it increase by 1 every time in the while loop. While your variable is less than or equal to 4,<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">program your CoDrone to fly forward and then turn left (or vice versa).<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wondering why you\u2019re starting at 0? Humans begin counting at 1, but computers begin counting at 0!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1575&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b99eb\" name=\"6a221541b99eb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program a forever loop with a while loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can program a while loop to run like a forever loop, which will repeat the code inside of it forever! All you<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">need to do is set the condition to &#8220;While code is running&#8221;, and then make sure you have an emergency stop (as you always<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">should!). You can also see what happens when you set the condition to false just by selecting that option<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">from the drop-down menu. Try both loops with your CoDrone\u2019s eye LEDs!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;6596&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1577&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may notice that the colors are switching very quickly. Add some Wait blocks from the timing section in<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">between switching colors.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;6597&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b9a35\" name=\"6a221541b9a35\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Until loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Until loops are a lot like while loops, except they\u2019ll run the code inside the block until the condition is true.<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each time the program runs through the while loop, it checks to see if the condition is true. If it is, the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">program will exit the loop, but after it finishes running that block of code one last time.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1580&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b9a7b\" name=\"6a221541b9a7b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Program an until loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Set your variable to 0, and then have it increase by 1 every time in the while loop. Program your drone so that<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">until your variable gets to 8, it will turn 1 second to either the left or right.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1581&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221541b9ae2\" name=\"6a221541b9ae2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Disco Drone<\/b><b>\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Program your drone to turn like a disco ball with its eye and arm LEDs changing color!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Rules:<\/b><b>\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You must use at least one loop in your program.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Both the eyes and arms must change colors at least once.<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don\u2019t forget a kill switch!<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 What are loops? [vc_column_text]Loops 